\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The V4 result is bounded rather than globally positive. (a) Equal- family smooth LER places Window and static MAP below \textsc  {Route-A}{}; the oracle is truth-privileged. Error bars are seed-cluster 95\% intervals. (b) Only the periodic EWMA-minus-\textsc  {Route-A}{} contrast survived Holm correction. (c) Tail non-inferiority required frequent fallback and unnecessary-fallback signals. (d) Under calibration shift, \textsc  {Route-A}{} matched EWMA at 181 errors in the worst 512-decision window, while static MAP had 32. Source: frozen T6.7.1 and T6.7.2 machine artifacts; plotted-source rows and hashes accompany the figure.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v4-evidence-boundary}{{2}{11}{The V4 result is bounded rather than globally positive. (a) Equal- family smooth LER places Window and static MAP below \RouteA {}; the oracle is truth-privileged. Error bars are seed-cluster 95\% intervals. (b) Only the periodic EWMA-minus-\RouteA {} contrast survived Holm correction. (c) Tail non-inferiority required frequent fallback and unnecessary-fallback signals. (d) Under calibration shift, \RouteA {} matched EWMA at 181 errors in the worst 512-decision window, while static MAP had 32. Source: frozen T6.7.1 and T6.7.2 machine artifacts; plotted-source rows and hashes accompany the figure}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {6.6}Causal-headroom audit and V5 early stop}{12}{subsection.6.6}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Why V5 was stopped before implementation. (a) Large diagnostic oracle headroom grows with access to unavailable truth. (b) Deployable selectors do not approach the registered 10\% entry level. (c) Hard and expanded truth oracles are almost identical; the new action family contributes 0.02549\%, far below the 12\% action-space gate. The logarithmic axis retains the small positive value. (d) The selector-to-oracle regret is dominated by estimation/activation (76.46\%), not action-space capacity (0.14\%). Source: T6.10.1 causal-headroom JSON/CSV; percentages are independently recomputed by the plotting script.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-headroom-stop}{{3}{12}{Why V5 was stopped before implementation. (a) Large diagnostic oracle headroom grows with access to unavailable truth. (b) Deployable selectors do not approach the registered 10\% entry level. (c) Hard and expanded truth oracles are almost identical; the new action family contributes 0.02549\%, far below the 12\% action-space gate. The logarithmic axis retains the small positive value. (d) The selector-to-oracle regret is dominated by estimation/activation (76.46\%), not action-space capacity (0.14\%). Source: T6.10.1 causal-headroom JSON/CSV; percentages are independently recomputed by the plotting script}{figure.3}{}}
